{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#132","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#132","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#132\",\"parent_revision\":\"7c818414535354228e20c1a28cadd505c9252eff1989bf646ae63a29e4d75d9f\",\"root_revision\":\"7c818414535354228e20c1a28cadd505c9252eff1989bf646ae63a29e4d75d9f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [x] The agent-frontmatter boundary accepts omitted, `null`, scalar-string, empty-list, and string-sequence forms.\\n- [x] Scalar strings and string sequences produce the same normalized `list[str]` values as the audited Claude Code filesystem loader.\\n- [x] `model_dump()` and the fixer-facing representation retain the authored scalar-versus-sequence shape; normalization is not used to rewrite source implicitly.\\n- [x] `AG003` does not report scalar strings as invalid.\\n- [x] A present number, boolean, or mapping produces one `AG003` warning explaining that Claude Code ignores the value and preloads no skill from it.\\n- [x] A sequence containing non-string members produces one `AG003` warning explaining that those members are discarded.\\n- [x] The same defect is not also reported as generic `FM005`.\\n- [x] `AG003` is non-fixable. skilllint does not guess intended skill names for discarded values.\\n- [x] `skilllint check --fix` preserves the parsed `skills` value and YAML shape when another fix serializes frontmatter, and a second fix run is idempotent.\\n- [x] The rule runs for directly checked and recursively discovered personal, project, added-directory, and plugin agent files.\\n- [x] The rule does not run on `SKILL.md` and does not change `SkillFrontmatter.skills`.\\n- [x] AG rules are scoped to `platforms=[\\\"claude-code\\\"]` and are present in the rule inventory, Claude adapter metadata, README, and rule catalog.\\n- [x] `packages/skilllint/schemas/claude_code/v1.json` records `skills` as an optional agent field with current provenance without presenting the catalog entry as the active type validator.\\n- [x] Tests cover every behavior-table row, mixed lists, direct-file and directory scans, diagnostic cardinality, JSON/text reporters, SKILL.md isolation, and `--fix` round-tripping.\\n- [x] Full tests, formatting, lint, type checks, and the existing benchmark workflow pass without a reported regression. Local verification plus the PR Test and Benchmark workflows pass.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nValidation of Markdown agent files follows Claude Code's **filesystem frontmatter contract**, not the stricter `--agents` / Agent SDK contract. A scalar string is supported in an agent file and must not produce an error.\\n\\nThe original list-only premise was based on the documented example rather than the file loader. PR #147 has been revised to implement the filesystem behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Surface | Contract |\\n|---|---|\\n| Markdown agent frontmatter | Accepts a scalar string or a sequence containing strings and normalizes those strings to a list |\\n| `--agents` JSON and Agent SDK `AgentDefinition.skills` | Requires `string[]` |\\n| Claude Code documentation | Shows the canonical YAML-sequence form but does not state that scalar file syntax is invalid |\\n\\nVerified against the published [Claude Code 2.1.251 package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@anthropic-ai/claude-code/v/2.1.251). The file loader and programmatic input use distinct schemas. The [subagent documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#preload-skills-into-subagents) supplies the field semantics and canonical example; the [Agent SDK documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/subagents) describes the separate programmatic contract.\\n\\nThe reproducible package hashes, npm integrity values, binary build ID, byte offsets, commands, behavior matrix, and audit limitations are recorded in [the checked-in runtime contract](https://github.com/bitflight-devops/skilllint/blob/feat/ag-agent-file-series/docs/runtime-contracts/claude-code-agent-skills-2.1.251.md).\\n\\nFor filesystem agents, the audited loader behavior is:\\n\\n| Source value | Loader result | Expected skilllint result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| omitted, `null`, empty string, or `[]` | no preloaded skills | clean |\\n| scalar string | normalized string list | clean |\\n| sequence of strings | normalized string list | clean |\\n| number, boolean, or mapping | value discarded; no preloaded skills | one warning |\\n| sequence containing non-string members | string members retained and normalized; other members discarded | one warning |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Actual Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBefore #147's revision:\\n\\n- `AgentFrontmatter.skills` was `str | None`.\\n- `normalize_comma_separated` flattened a sequence into a CSV string, so the model preserved neither the authored YAML shape nor Claude Code's normalized-list semantics.\\n- `_normalize_tool_fields_and_detect_changes` restored the original `skills` value as a compensating workaround.\\n- Values Claude Code discards could pass skilllint without a useful diagnostic.\\n\\nValid YAML lists already passed lint and the restore-original guard protected them from known `--fix` corruption. The demonstrated user impact was silent false negatives for ineffective declarations plus an inaccurate internal boundary model, not current corruption of valid files.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Represent the supported filesystem input forms without lossy list-to-CSV coercion.\\n- Keep the authored value available for safe serialization while exposing normalized `list[str]` semantics to typed consumers when needed.\\n- Accept scalar strings and string sequences without a diagnostic.\\n- Warn only when Claude Code discards all or part of the supplied value.\\n- Preserve `skills` unchanged when fixing unrelated fields.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Non Goals\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Enforcing the documented YAML-sequence style as a correctness error.\\n- Validating the separate `--agents` JSON or Agent SDK input contract.\\n- Checking whether a named skill exists, is enabled, or can be preloaded.\\n- Defining `skills` for AgentSkills `SKILL.md` or reviving FM008.\\n- Changing agent `tools` or `disallowedTools`; those remain owned by #109.\\n- Adding opinions about duplicates, wildcard names, or delimiter style without separate evidence.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Relationships\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #105 removed FM008 from the wrong file family.\\n- #108 established that AgentSkills rules apply to `SKILL.md`, not Claude Code agent files.\\n- #109 owns the AG-series decision and agent tool-field rules.\\n- #147 implements this contract on head `6162cb2`; the issue remains open until the PR is merged.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f80311fe72a47e5a8d175ed8c678324bf413d1b7f6aaa1164b0035fbc586e564\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-r3g\"}"}